ce:section.ce:para:
We have selected 4 agricultural feedstock from 2 farms (see Table 1
                        ).

                              -

M1 is cattle manure from a farm located nearby Lyon (Monts du Lyonnais, Rhône, France);


                              -

M2 is cattle manure from a farm located in Ennezat (Puy de Dôme, France);


                              -

S is a mixture of maize and triticale silage from the same farm than M2;


                              -

SM is a mixture of silage S and cattle manure M2 used to feed the AD plant. According to the plant operator, the proportion of silage and manure was 1:3 in fresh weight.

All different samples (untreated and mechanically pretreated, lab-scale and full-scale) have been plotted according the two principal component (Fig. 5
                        ). From this plot, we have drawn 4 area (in color):

                              -

The red area (bottom left) entails all untreated samples (lab-scale);


                              -

The brown area contains all samples after simple shredding at lab scale (I-PT);


                              -

The green area contains all the samples after mixing at lab-scale (II-PT);


                              -

The blue-green area contains all the samples after blending at lab-scale (III-PT).
